WEBVTT

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:05.430
The Nadesico continues her journey to Mars.

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:07.860
The new pilots who just jointed us,

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.730
are, as expect, BAKA-bakka!.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:14.170
And some people on board are getting all excited on their own.

00:00:14.830 --> 00:00:18.600
I wonder, if they intend to do this seriously or not?

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:55.470
<b>Love</b>

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:56.130
Ai.

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:57.010
<b>Pity</b>

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:57.130
Ai.

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:57.950
<b>Indigo</b>

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:57.960
Ai.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:01:59.960
Lots of "Ai"'s...

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:07.290
Being the latest and greatest in technological advancements,

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:09.890
the Nadesico pretty much runs on auto-pilot except in emergencies.

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:11.400
To put it bluntly, there's nothing to do.

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:16.440
The only people who are sometimes needed are Megumi-san as communicator and I as operator.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:20.490
Minato-san, the helmswoman, is sleeping in late.

00:02:20.490 --> 00:02:22.120
Yep, I was up late so...

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:24.900
Oh well.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:29.750
Really, this is boring.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:36.170
Ruri-chan's "Navigation Logs"

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:37.690
Forth-Level Alert

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:38.510
Incoming enemy attack.

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.380
From where?!

00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:41.990
Intercept!

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:42.790
Not needed.

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:46.390
Distortion Field, operating normally.

00:02:48.330 --> 00:02:50.680
Since the battle at space colony,

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:57.450
The reason why they don't concentrate on attacking us is most likely to judge the capacity of this vessel.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:01.030
They will probably persist in taking pot shots at us

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:03.990
until we enter Mars space where they have air superiority over us.

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:06.700
What are your thoughts on this, Captain?

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:09.690
You're certainly sharp, for a kid.

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.090
I'm a young girl.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:13.050
Ah?!

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.190
Second wave of attack.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:17.090
Field strength stable.

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:22.180
I see. I don't have much to do until we get to Mars.

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:25.660
Captain, you're in the way.

00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:28.100
Please return to your seat.

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:29.420
Okay!

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:45.700
Captain, is something wrong?

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:48.260
No, nothing really!

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.490
It just looked to me as if you are very happy.

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:53.230
Oh, you can tell?

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:53.520
Eh?

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:56.120
Captain, you are still there?

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:59.800
We can't get this started until you come, so please hurry.

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:01.050
Oh, that's right!

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:03.830
Make sure to be dressed appropriately for this.

00:04:03.830 --> 00:04:04.780
All right!

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:08.100
Oops! Ouch!

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:12.860
For the next two weeks, while the enemy was relatively inactive,

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:17.500
funerals were held for all who perished in the previous battle.

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:28.570
Actually, Satsuki Midori 2 was almost a total loss.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.610
The bodies of those who died were lost in space.

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:34.250
Few of the remains will ever be recovered.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:38.690
That being the case, the civilian enterprise Nergal

00:04:38.690 --> 00:04:41.870
placed even greater significance on the funeral ceremony itself.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:48.200
I understand, but why do I have to be the one who does all this stuff?

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:50.610
Because it's the captain's duty

00:04:50.610 --> 00:04:52.560
to act as master of ceremonies for various events.

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:53.480
Hi...

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:57.810
Ichimai da, nimai da, sanmai da...

00:04:57.810 --> 00:04:59.410
Ha, oshimai da (it's over).

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:00.870
No, it isn't over.

00:05:01.730 --> 00:05:03.710
Come on, hurry, hurry!

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:04.660
Let me see...

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:06.660
Our Father who art in heaven...

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:07.350
Come on!

00:05:08.130 --> 00:05:08.990
That's done!

00:05:08.990 --> 00:05:10.160
Still more to come!

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:10.850
Eh?

00:05:10.850 --> 00:05:12.180
Hurry, hurry!

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:12.740
Hi..!

00:05:13.150 --> 00:05:14.200
We need to hustle!

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:15.160
Hurry!

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:15.950
Another one!

00:05:17.240 --> 00:05:18.980
The Earth is a small, yet very diverse place.

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:21.640
Diverse religions. Diverse customs.

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:23.420
And diverse funeral rituals that go along with them.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:26.720
But why do I have to do all this?

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:29.990
Well, the colony was a total loss.

00:05:29.990 --> 00:05:32.050
It's the Nadesico's job to carry out the funerals.

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:39.930
We can't afford to have Buddhist monks or Shinto priests aboard, so the captain has to be the substitute.

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:41.020
Exactly.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:45.220
It's hard to cut costs with weddings and funerals.

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:49.830
But I haven't seen Akito lately.

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:51.370
I haven't talked to him.

00:05:52.330 --> 00:05:55.200
Come on, we're going to take care of at least five today!

00:05:56.440 --> 00:05:58.660
By the way, our contract features benefits

00:05:58.660 --> 00:06:00.920
that are not normally tolerated in the armed services.

00:06:01.610 --> 00:06:03.340
We are the children of the sun!

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:04.310
Sunshine! Moonlight! . . . . . Sunshine! Moonlight!

00:06:04.310 --> 00:06:06.860
We respect the religion and ideology of the individual.

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:09.850
Regarding funerals, that take place all too often in times of war,

00:06:09.850 --> 00:06:13.260
we do our best to fulfill the last wishes of the deceased

00:06:13.260 --> 00:06:13.540
Sunshine! Moonlight! . . . . . Sunshine! Moonlight!

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:14.710
Another four to go!

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:16.170
Another three.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:17.630
Another two.

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:19.100
Last one.

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:22.500
It's finally over.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:26.140
Captain, the hat.

00:06:26.850 --> 00:06:29.510
All this just for being the captain?

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:33.420
There are many more requests for personalized funeral services.

00:06:34.560 --> 00:06:36.360
Open data display window.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.150
I don't need a funeral or grave.

00:06:39.150 --> 00:06:40.420
Thank goodness.

00:06:40.450 --> 00:06:43.630
Just scatter my ashes over the vast blue ocean.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:46.550
Ocean? How are we going to do that out here?

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:47.780
Next request.

00:06:48.300 --> 00:06:49.490
My wish...

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:52.450
I want to become star in the Milky Way

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:54.230
wishing for everyone's happiness.

00:06:54.230 --> 00:06:54.700
I understand how she feels, but...

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:56.180
La la la la la la.

00:06:56.180 --> 00:06:59.080
Should we have her gravestone shaped like a star?

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:01.470
My wish is

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:04.060
to be bitten in the neck by the most beautiful woman on Earth.

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:04.420
While having a stake driven into my chest. I want her to...

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:06.880
Captain, are you the most beautiful woman on Earth?

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:07.480
While having a stake driven into my chest. I want her to...

00:07:08.550 --> 00:07:11.400
There are still many more requests for personalized funeral services.

00:07:12.310 --> 00:07:13.840
This many?

00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:15.350
Yes, this many.

00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:18.400
This many more funerals?!

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:20.910
This is only part of them.

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:25.400
I suppose it goes to show just how many people died in that battle.

00:07:26.620 --> 00:07:34.060
Lots of funerals for lots of people.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:36.260
The only thing I can do is..

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:37.850
funerals.

00:07:39.090 --> 00:07:40.170
left to mourn?!

00:07:41.530 --> 00:07:43.830
Ah, If you are master of ceremonies.

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:45.690
Will you do weddings too?

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:51.950
You're pretty cruel, Megumi-san.

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:53.370
Am I?

00:07:53.720 --> 00:07:54.680
Yes, you are.

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:56.190
Am I?

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:57.520
Yes, you are.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:58.940
Am I?

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:00.470
Yes, you are.

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:05.000
I guess I am cruel.

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:09.670
All right, here we go!

00:08:10.850 --> 00:08:13.010
Once the funerals are over, next come the receptions.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:14.840
Funeral manju and bento.

00:08:14.840 --> 00:08:17.430
Don't disappoint the dead with the meal prepared in their honor.

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:21.250
For them, this is the last and final banquet!

00:08:22.590 --> 00:08:24.420
Reconfirming today's deceased!

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:27.070
Italians, Arabs, Russians and Thai!

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:31.070
For Tom Yum Kung you don't use soy sauce but Nampra!

00:08:32.220 --> 00:08:33.370
What's that?

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:35.150
It's soy sauce made from fish.

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:38.900
The Earth is small, yet still very vast!

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:42.550
Each region has it's own flavors.
Let me see... Nampra, Nampra...

00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:45.170
Not to be boastful, but here at the Nadesico Cafeteria,

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:47.600
we have over three hundred different spices and flavorings.

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:49.870
I can't find the Nampra.

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:53.310
Tenkawa, you sure are a klutz!

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:54.310
Is it there?

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:55.090
Nope.

00:08:55.230 --> 00:08:56.500
Is it there?

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:57.300
Nope.

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:59.210
Then the rest would be in there!

00:08:59.700 --> 00:09:01.970
Come on, hurry it up! lt'll boil over!

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:05.810
All right, here we go again today!

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:07.210
Right..!

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:08.370
Akito...

00:09:08.370 --> 00:09:09.810
Move it! Move it!

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:10.410
Delivery

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:11.650
Funeral food coming through!

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:12.980
Move it! Move it!

00:09:13.370 --> 00:09:20.090
Akito!

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:20.830
Yurika!

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:22.470
You're the captain.

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:26.210
You need to fulfill your duty to those who have perished.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:28.310
Akito...

00:09:28.800 --> 00:09:30.430
You're so mean, Akito.

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:31.740
Move it! Move it!

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:33.710
Move it!

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:36.670
I get it. He was cheering me on!

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:39.110
"Pull yourself together! You're the captain!"

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:39.940
That must be it!

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:42.330
That's right. I have to fight on!

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:45.140
I need to get through this, so I can talk to Akito.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:48.350
I humbly mourn all your deaths!

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:51.690
Yurika sure is into it today.

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:54.690
Akito! Wait for me, Akito!

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:57.210
No more...

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:01.830
Captain, the hat.

00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:05.030
But I'm so tired.

00:10:05.550 --> 00:10:08.030
Ruri-chan, I wonder what it means to be a captain?

00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:09.290
Would you like to know?

00:10:09.290 --> 00:10:10.620
Yeah, I want to know.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:13.550
I can't teach you, but I can gather together the data.

00:10:14.810 --> 00:10:16.670
Omoikane, collect data.

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:19.020
Search data library.

00:10:19.020 --> 00:10:20.960
Analysis of trends in the characteristics of captains.

00:10:21.510 --> 00:10:22.960
You're something, Ruri-chan.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:24.100
The reply.

00:10:24.800 --> 00:10:26.700
It's asking for captains of what era?

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:28.150
The last hundred years.

00:10:29.180 --> 00:10:32.560
Searching

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:34.020
Searching complete

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:35.140
Done.

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:38.450
Analysis of current trends in captains.

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:43.270
Since the conclusion of the Second World War, no noteworthy captains have been recorded.

00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:47.250
In this age, combat has been fully worked into overall war strategy,

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:50.120
and the decisions made by the captain of a single ship cannot elicit a reversal

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:51.540
in the strategic flow of events in battle.

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:55.180
The main duty of a captain is to be a figurehead for the warship

00:10:55.180 --> 00:11:00.170
who can comfortably absorb the frustrations and stresses that the combatants must contend with.

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:05.740
Previously, reliable-looking elderly men, who could project an image of resolve and calm, were popular.

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:07.590
But recently to motivate the contemporary youth,

00:11:07.590 --> 00:11:10.770
there has been a marked increase in the number of handsome female and male captains.

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:16.440
In other words, true captains, with skills such as tactical mastery or intelligent decision making

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:17.870
are no longer really needed.

00:11:18.550 --> 00:11:20.240
What does that mean?

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:22.500
That means... That means...

00:11:23.360 --> 00:11:26.160
It means it really doesn't matter who the captain is anymore.

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:30.990
Megumi-san...

00:11:32.010 --> 00:11:33.260
I know.

00:11:33.260 --> 00:11:34.990
I'm cruel, I guess.

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:36.220
Yes.

00:11:38.160 --> 00:11:39.950
But how can I help it?

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:48.720
Thank you for your guidance, Ma'am!

00:11:49.100 --> 00:11:50.420
Nice work, girls.

00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:52.160
See you tomorrow!

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:53.040
Eri-chan...

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:53.770
Where is Tenkawa?

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:56.930
I saw him staring at the spice rack in the storage room.

00:11:57.880 --> 00:11:58.680
Tenkawa!

00:11:59.040 --> 00:11:59.900
Yes, Chef?

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:02.630
Haven't you seen a spice rack before?

00:12:02.630 --> 00:12:05.360
Yes, but you see, I was raised on Mars.

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:08.580
I never realized that there were this many spices on Earth.

00:12:10.150 --> 00:12:16.280
There was a time when each region, each city, each village

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:18.600
and even each family had their own unique flavoring.

00:12:19.070 --> 00:12:20.590
They called them "your mother's flavoring".

00:12:20.860 --> 00:12:24.890
But this isn't a high-class restaurant.

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:27.890
Why do you do all this for a cafeteria on a warship?

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:30.600
It's because this is a warship.

00:12:32.130 --> 00:12:35.680
This happened back in the days when limited skirmishes were breaking out

00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:37.020
between the Moon and the Earth.

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:41.390
A young soldier who was about to die asked me in a weakened voice,

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:44.300
"May I have some Paella for the last time?"

00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:45.700
Paella?

00:12:46.020 --> 00:12:50.100
But back then, all I could prepare decently were Chinese dishes.

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:55.300
All I could give him was something more like botched fried rice,

00:12:55.300 --> 00:12:56.560
but he ate some of it and said,

00:12:56.990 --> 00:12:58.960
"Thank you, it was delicious,

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:02.100
but it tasted different than my mom's."

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:08.550
Back in those days I didn't know what Paella was, nor that a saffron flower gives that dish its flavor.

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:11.930
Then that soldier passed on.

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:13.840
This is war, where you can die any day.

00:13:13.840 --> 00:13:17.420
That's why I at least want to be ready for their last meal.

00:13:17.420 --> 00:13:20.190
Being able to make real Paella with a true saffron fragrance.

00:13:21.340 --> 00:13:23.650
That's what's behind that spice rack.

00:13:24.240 --> 00:13:25.550
I want to be a cook!

00:13:25.940 --> 00:13:27.690
An even better cook!

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:30.610
You've got something even more important to do!

00:13:31.570 --> 00:13:34.070
Thank you for the great work, evening shift workers!

00:13:34.070 --> 00:13:36.160
Night shift workers, please do your best again!

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:38.400
The current time is ten o'clock.

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:42.530
Everyone tells me that I need to fight.

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:43.560
But...

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:47.530
No! I don't want to fight!

00:13:47.530 --> 00:13:49.070
I want to be a cook!

00:13:49.490 --> 00:13:51.830
Do people want me to fight anyway?

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:53.160
To fight regardless?

00:13:53.460 --> 00:13:53.950
Right
Left

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:55.320
Ready? Go!

00:13:55.320 --> 00:13:58.390
Right
Left

00:14:01.580 --> 00:14:03.150
Ruri-chan, Ruri-chan...

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:03.990
Yes?

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:06.880
I haven't seen the Captain lately. Where has she been?

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:08.890
You probably scared her away.

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:11.270
I'm worried. Let's take a look.

00:14:15.690 --> 00:14:16.470
There she is.

00:14:16.470 --> 00:14:18.600
No, that's Minato-san.

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:19.460
Oh, I'm stuffed.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:21.110
And the Captain?

00:14:21.110 --> 00:14:21.550
Okay.

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:26.010
The meditation room?

00:14:26.330 --> 00:14:29.530
Zen Meditating

00:14:30.290 --> 00:14:31.010
I must meditate.

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:34.170
What is the meaning of being a captain?

00:14:34.170 --> 00:14:36.720
What shall I do as a captain?!

00:14:45.330 --> 00:14:46.780
What is she thinking?

00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:48.700
What's wrong?

00:14:48.700 --> 00:14:51.170
The captain has gone on sabbatical.

00:14:51.170 --> 00:14:53.740
Sabbatical?

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:57.910
Right, so it is the executive officer's duty to assume the captain's functions.

00:14:58.210 --> 00:14:59.360
Please accept!

00:14:59.920 --> 00:15:01.330
Dear friend, sleep well!

00:15:01.680 --> 00:15:01.900
Thank God the funerals can be carried out without a hindrance.

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:06.690
Bear, bear, bear, bear, bear! Bear...

00:15:06.690 --> 00:15:09.670
We'll leave the Captain to work out her issues.

00:15:10.570 --> 00:15:14.260
And so two weeks went by as we quickly neared Mars.

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:16.970
But the Captain...

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:18.680
Meditate...

00:15:19.520 --> 00:15:22.970
Gautama Siddhartha obtained enlightenment under a bodhi tree.

00:15:22.970 --> 00:15:25.010
I want to reach enlightenment too.

00:15:25.340 --> 00:15:26.690
I must cast aside all my worldly passions!

00:15:27.910 --> 00:15:28.650
What are my worldly passions?

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:30.850
<b>Worldly Passion</b>

00:15:30.850 --> 00:15:31.860
Desire!

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:33.780
My worldly passions...

00:15:34.080 --> 00:15:34.920
My...

00:15:36.740 --> 00:15:38.050
Akito!

00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:41.420
Akito likes me a lot, right?

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:42.720
What are you saying!

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:45.290
Akito likes me!

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:46.290
Stop it!

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:50.010
That's right! Akito loves me!

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:52.460
You don't need to be shy.

00:15:52.460 --> 00:15:54.320
Akito likes me!

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:55.820
Who told you that?

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:59.700
I don't need to hear it from anyone. Akito likes me!

00:15:59.700 --> 00:16:00.210
Hey...

00:16:00.210 --> 00:16:01.380
Is that so?

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:11.390
Akito-san is mine.

00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:18.410
Wait! Come back here!

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:26.470
Wait! Wait, Akito! Come back!

00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:29.860
Wait, Akito! Where are you going?! Akito!

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:30.990
He's mine.

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:36.260
What is this?! What's going on?!

00:16:36.260 --> 00:16:37.360
This isn't going to happen!

00:16:37.360 --> 00:16:39.330
No, no, no, no!

00:16:39.670 --> 00:16:42.810
Cast aside extraneous thoughts.

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:45.150
They are reflected in your brain waves. Very bad.

00:16:45.150 --> 00:16:46.570
Cast aside extraneous thoughts.

00:16:48.890 --> 00:16:51.890
Cast aside my worldly passions.

00:16:51.890 --> 00:16:52.880
Cast aside my...

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:54.390
I don't want to fight!

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:57.430
I... I...

00:16:57.930 --> 00:16:59.040
Akito!

00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:01.000
What's going on here?!

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:02.100
Is this the real thing?

00:17:02.400 --> 00:17:03.650
What are you doing here?

00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:07.170
I was fighting my worldly passions in order to reach enlightenment.

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:08.890
But then Akito came!

00:17:08.890 --> 00:17:10.380
I'm no worldly passion!

00:17:11.070 --> 00:17:14.080
I had something on my mind. So I came here to...

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:16.550
I understand. Akito likes me.

00:17:17.360 --> 00:17:19.180
What the hell are you saying?

00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:21.690
I can tell! Akito likes me!

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:24.150
You were thinking about that in here?

00:17:24.150 --> 00:17:25.390
I see the light now.

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:28.850
You like me, not because of some worldly passion,

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:33.430
but because this is a grand and noble love taking shape!

00:17:33.430 --> 00:17:35.740
Worldly passions. Worldly passions. Worldly passions.

00:17:36.730 --> 00:17:37.770
Oh, a worldly passion.

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:39.730
Captain, we have a mutiny!

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:42.990
Some of the crew have mutinied.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:45.080
Who's in charge here?!

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:49.750
We will oppose by all possible means Nergal's...

00:17:50.550 --> 00:17:52.000
Sorry about this, Megu-chan.

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:57.510
What's the matter, everyone?

00:17:58.480 --> 00:18:00.960
We know you'll perform funerals for us,

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:03.840
but we didn't know about this.

00:18:03.840 --> 00:18:05.390
But it says in the contract...

00:18:05.670 --> 00:18:09.300
Who in this day and age takes the time to read the entire contract?!

00:18:09.300 --> 00:18:09.810
See?

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:13.010
Wow, this is small type.

00:18:13.010 --> 00:18:15.430
Read the smallest type of all on that page.

00:18:16.180 --> 00:18:20.390
"While we do not prohibit fraternization between employees,

00:18:20.390 --> 00:18:25.080
for public morality, any act of intimacy beyond holding hands is prohibited."

00:18:25.080 --> 00:18:26.120
What's this?

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:27.490
As you read.

00:18:27.490 --> 00:18:28.660
Now you see?

00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:32.360
"Holding hands?" Is the Nadesico a preschool?

00:18:32.360 --> 00:18:33.520
Do you actually think healthy young people

00:18:33.520 --> 00:18:36.320
will be satisfied with holding hands?

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:37.640
I'm still young.

00:18:37.960 --> 00:18:38.700
You are?

00:18:38.700 --> 00:18:39.960
I am!

00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:42.070
A young couple look closely at one another.

00:18:42.070 --> 00:18:43.200
As they stare into each other's eyes...

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:43.850
Their lips close in?

00:18:44.150 --> 00:18:46.180
For the young couple's love is all too innocent.

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:47.980
But the two quickly move on to less innocent intimacy.

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:49.750
How I wish to be held so close! To be held so tightly!

00:18:50.050 --> 00:18:52.860
Exactly, that escalation is the whole problem.

00:18:52.860 --> 00:18:54.150
You bastard!

00:18:54.770 --> 00:18:58.830
If the couple eventually gets married, that will cost money.

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:01.780
And what will happen if children result?

00:19:01.780 --> 00:19:05.060
The Nadesico is not a preschool.

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:06.240
Shut up! Shut up!

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:10.170
Listen, space is vast, and people are free to fall in love.

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:12.330
Limited to holding hands?

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:15.670
It would be better to be stuck at home with my wife!

00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:17.760
Well, you have validated the contract by...

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:18.590
Shut up!

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:20.590
See this?

00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:22.800
Please examine the contract as well.

00:19:25.610 --> 00:19:26.530
What should I do?

00:19:29.220 --> 00:19:31.270
We should be nearing Mars pretty soon.

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:37.390
What the hell?!

00:19:37.390 --> 00:19:38.790
Ruri-chan, what about the field?

00:19:38.790 --> 00:19:39.570
It's still up.

00:19:39.980 --> 00:19:42.890
This attack isn't like the ones before.

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:44.330
We need to intercept and neutralize.

00:19:54.670 --> 00:19:55.840
Everyone, listen to me.

00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:58.670
I am well aware of your frustrations with the contract.

00:19:58.980 --> 00:20:00.730
But this is not the time to address that issue!

00:20:01.280 --> 00:20:03.940
Unless we win... Unless we win...

00:20:04.250 --> 00:20:05.090
Lots of funerals.

00:20:05.690 --> 00:20:07.470
I will not have that! No!

00:20:08.050 --> 00:20:11.460
I'd rather be doing weddings than funerals!

00:20:13.880 --> 00:20:15.880
Launching Aestivalis units!

00:20:15.880 --> 00:20:16.460
Here we go!

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:17.040
Hi!

00:20:17.040 --> 00:20:17.400
Okay!

00:20:19.670 --> 00:20:22.480
In order to live on, we need to end the fighting!

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:24.280
But, I...

00:20:27.970 --> 00:20:31.950
So the Nadesico's battles at Mars began.

00:20:32.800 --> 00:20:36.190
But somehow I don't like contracts that grownups sign.

00:20:36.750 --> 00:20:38.430
I don't want to grow up to be like them.

00:20:39.140 --> 00:20:41.210
That was how I felt today.

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:46.870
Since the dawn of history, mankind has projected various images on Mars.

00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:48.020
Some have seen a symbol of war.

00:21:48.020 --> 00:21:49.920
Others thought octopus-like people lived there.

00:21:49.920 --> 00:21:51.670
For some, it was where the beautiful Martian princess reigned.

00:21:51.670 --> 00:21:54.840
And Schiaparelli and Lowell saw canals.

00:21:54.840 --> 00:21:57.780
Wave after wave of enemy attacks pummel the Nadesico.

00:21:57.780 --> 00:21:59.530
Look forward to having your senses excited

00:21:59.530 --> 00:22:02.570
by the newly developed love, love super sound system!

00:22:02.570 --> 00:22:04.510
It's the final climax! Or maybe not.

00:22:04.770 --> 00:22:06.920
Next Martian Successor Nadesico:

00:22:06.990 --> 00:22:09.310
"Sort of Like a Fateful Decision"

00:22:09.640 --> 00:22:11.460
Let's watch it, everyone!
